  "term": "microaggression",
  "definition": "A microaggression is a brief comment, action, or situation that conveys a hostile, insulting, or negative slight toward someone. It can be deliberate or unintentional and includes openly discriminatory acts, subtle demeaning messages, and dismissals or negations of a person’s identity or thoughts.",
